Presidential elections were held in [[Moldova]] on 17 November 1996, with a second round on 1 December.<ref name=NS>[[Dieter Nohlen]] & Philip Stöver (2010) ''Elections in Europe: A data handbook'', p1330 {{ISBN|978-3-8329-5609-7}}</ref> Whilst incumbent President [[Mircea Snegur]] received the most votes in the first round, he was defeated in the second by [[Petru Lucinschi]].<ref>Nohlen & Stöver, p1343</ref> It was the first contested presidential election in Moldovan history, the first Moldovan presidential election in which an incumbent lost re-election, and the last direct presidential election until [[2016 Moldovan presidential election|2016]].

